.TH X301-CRYPTO-POLICY 8 "September 2026" "x301-openssl-provider" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
x301-crypto-policy \- change crypto policy while preserving X301 integration
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B x301-crypto-policy set
.I POLICY
.br
.B x301-crypto-policy
.RB { reconcile | enable | disable | status }
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B x301-crypto-policy
updates the system crypto policy and the X301 OpenSSL group overlay as one
transaction. Use it instead of calling
.B update-crypto-policies
directly while x301-openssl-provider is installed.
.PP
X301 and X301MLKEM1024 are experimental, non-standardized, and not FIPS
validated. Their activation invalidates claims that a restrictive policy
contains only its named algorithms.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI "set " POLICY
Select POLICY and reconcile the X301 group overlay.
.TP
.B reconcile
Rebuild and verify the overlay for the currently selected policy.
.TP
.B enable
Alias for
.BR reconcile .
.TP
.B disable
Disable the X301 group override and rebuild the selected policy.
.TP
.B status
Print the overlay state and selected crypto policy.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/crypto-policies/local.d/opensslcnf-zz-x301.config
X301 OpenSSL group overlay.
.TP
.I /etc/pki/tls/openssl.d/x301-provider.conf
OpenSSL provider activation.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR update-crypto-policies (8),
.BR openssl (1)
